<title>UK: Racal up after positive press comment.</title>
<headline>Racal up after positive press comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Racal Electronics Plc rose in active trading on Monday after upbeat comment on the stock in the Sunday Times, traders said.</p>
<p>Racal shares were up 4p at 290 by 1302 GMT in volume of 5.2 million shares, making it the eighth most active stock in the London market.</p>
<p>The paper said Friday's bid by Williams Holdings Plc for Chubb Security Plc, demerged from Racal in 1992, showed the ability of Racal chairman Sir Ernest Harrison to deliver shareholder value and advised Chubb shareholders to switch into the stock. Chubb was down 3p at 421-1/2.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
